but also considering,

00:08:29.320 --> 00:08:31.960
within product, how can
we do some A/B testing

00:08:31.960 --> 00:08:35.710
to drive higher LTV couples
into a more relevant experience

00:08:35.710 --> 00:08:39.559
and drive a lot of
personalization?

00:08:39.559 --> 00:08:41.870
Something I just
figured out yesterday

00:08:41.870 --> 00:08:46.910
was the partnership with
certain hotels on the websites.

00:08:46.910 --> 00:08:50.090
Like, you can see
who else is going

00:08:50.090 --> 00:08:53.743
to that wedding is going to
be staying at certain hotels.

00:08:53.743 --> 00:08:55.160
And I didn't know
if that's, like,

00:08:55.160 --> 00:08:58.430
another way of
driving revenue too.

00:08:58.430 --> 00:09:00.140
Yeah, so we do have--

00:09:00.140 --> 00:09:03.020
in terms of our revenue streams,
there are a few different ones.

00:09:03.020 --> 00:09:07.010
And when a couple
comes into our platform

00:09:07.010 --> 00:09:09.650
and they become a member, they
can create a wedding website.

00:09:09.650 --> 00:09:12.050
And the website itself
doesn't inherently

00:09:12.050 --> 00:09:13.250
drive any value for us.

00:09:13.250 --> 00:09:16.370
That's almost like a free
offering that we offer.

00:09:16.370 --> 00:09:18.592
But then if you consider,
like, attaching a registry

00:09:18.592 --> 00:09:21.050
and then talking through the
commissions that are built off

00:09:21.050 --> 00:09:23.208
of that one or
something like that,

00:09:23.208 --> 00:09:24.500
start to get into some of them.

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:28.220
And then a lot of it is
our primary business model

00:09:28.220 --> 00:09:33.560
we're focused on is on the
overall wedding experience

00:09:33.560 --> 00:09:36.140
and helping couples
do what it is

00:09:36.140 --> 00:09:39.080
they need to do to plan that
huge moment in your life.

00:09:39.080 --> 00:09:42.170
So that could be what types
of paper do you need to buy,

00:09:42.170 --> 00:09:45.530
which is like, invites, save
the dates, thank you cards,

00:09:45.530 --> 00:09:47.960
et cetera, or building
out a registry.

00:09:47.960 --> 00:09:52.250
Or the harder challenge is
when you're planning a wedding,

00:09:52.250 --> 00:09:54.170
there's a lot of different
vendors and venues

00:09:54.170 --> 00:09:55.753
