00:11:15.870 --> 00:11:18.300
So, as you start
getting through,

00:11:18.300 --> 00:11:21.030
you can kind of consider the
different journeys that people

00:11:21.030 --> 00:11:23.700
are going on based on not
only just the time since they

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:26.400
registered but also the time
since they're getting married.

00:11:26.400 --> 00:11:28.200
And that kind of
allows a good means

00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:31.130
of personalization in
terms of sending people

00:11:31.130 --> 00:11:32.880
on the appropriate
journey that's relevant

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:35.460
for them based on both of those
different event dates that

00:11:35.460 --> 00:11:38.650
are happening.

00:11:38.650 --> 00:11:41.180
I see, Katherine, you put
a question into the chat.

00:11:41.180 --> 00:11:42.550
Do you want to jump in?

00:11:42.550 --> 00:11:45.070
KATHERINE GERTON:
Yeah, I was curious

00:11:45.070 --> 00:11:47.230
as to what your
analytics of-- you

00:11:47.230 --> 00:11:49.960
know, speaking of wedding
season, the lack of wedding

00:11:49.960 --> 00:11:54.723
season during the last
several years due to COVID.

00:11:54.723 --> 00:11:56.140
