00:16:13.570 --> 00:16:16.210
Yeah, we're very
mixed right now.

00:16:16.210 --> 00:16:21.130
We have-- I think a lot of our
production code is living in R,

00:16:21.130 --> 00:16:23.380
and a majority of the
analytics that are happening

00:16:23.380 --> 00:16:27.610
are in R. We do have a fair
amount that's also in Python.

00:16:27.610 --> 00:16:30.400
That's one of the reasons that
I really like the reframing

00:16:30.400 --> 00:16:31.590
from RStudio Deposit.

00:16:31.590 --> 00:16:33.340
It's kind of like it's
just all inclusive.

00:16:33.340 --> 00:16:34.798
You can focus on
anything you want.

00:16:34.798 --> 00:16:37.368
I think if you're focused on
what language you're using,

00:16:37.368 --> 00:16:39.160
you're less focused on
the business problem

00:16:39.160 --> 00:16:41.240
that you're trying to solve.

00:16:41.240 --> 00:16:43.360
So I definitely like
the reframing there.

00:16:43.360 --> 00:16:46.083
But yeah, we do have a specific
amount of codebase built out

00:16:46.083 --> 00:16:46.750
in both of them.

00:16:51.847 --> 00:16:53.930
I think you asked a question
