on specific events
that are actually

00:45:11.132 --> 00:45:12.340
happening within our website.

00:45:15.250 --> 00:45:19.128
And just to double check, CDP,
that's Customer Data Profile?

00:45:19.128 --> 00:45:20.170
Customer Data Platform.

00:45:20.170 --> 00:45:21.030
RACHEL DEMPSEY: Or platform.

00:45:21.030 --> 00:45:21.530
OK.

00:45:21.530 --> 00:45:23.410
So it's like a
singular location

00:45:23.410 --> 00:45:27.175
to store profiling variables
about customers that you know

00:45:27.175 --> 00:45:29.140
as well as all of the
actions that are actually

00:45:29.140 --> 00:45:30.550
happening within your website.

00:45:30.550 --> 00:45:34.840
And you can build filters
and do custom SQL traits

00:45:34.840 --> 00:45:37.510
and really get a good
perspective about how people

00:45:37.510 --> 00:45:39.700
are interacting and then
build custom journeys

00:45:39.700 --> 00:45:43.130
based on how those interactions
are actually happening.

00:45:43.130 --> 00:45:43.790
Cool.

00:45:43.790 --> 00:45:45.440
Thank you.

00:45:45.440 --> 00:45:46.980
There is an anonymous question.

00:45:46.980 --> 00:45:49.100
